    hpi: "Judith Nzomo, a 77-year-old Social Worker from Nyeri, presents with a 3-week history of burning epigastric pain that comes on 2-3 hours after meals and is relieved by eating or taking antacids. Pain wakes him at night (~2 AM). Reports bloating and occasional nausea but no vomiting. Has been using an over-the-counter antacid mixture (Maalox) with temporary relief. Appetite is good and no weight loss. No NSAID use.",
