    difficulty: "Beginner",
    demographics: "Patrick Wambui, 82-year-old male, 66 kg, Chef from Bungoma",
    chiefComplaint: "Frequent heartburn, regurgitation, and sour taste in mouth for 2 months",
    hpi: "Patrick Wambui, a 82-year-old Chef from Bungoma, presents with retrosternal burning sensation (heartburn) occurring 30-60 minutes after meals, worse on lying down or bending forward. Reports acid regurgitation leaving a sour taste, occasional difficulty swallowing (dysphagia) with solid food, and chronic cough (worse at night). Symptoms started 2 months ago and have been increasing in frequency (now daily). Uses over-the-counter antacids with minimal relief. BMI 31 kg/m².",
    pmh: "Mild intermittent asthma. No prior GI surgery.",
    medHx: "No regular medications",
